# Advisories govulncheck reports as reached by the backend's code that the
# gate (scripts/govulncheck.sh) lets through. One id per line; say why, and
# when the line can go. Audit of 2026-10-15, plan S3.

# docker/docker v28.5.2: no fixed release exists. Both are in the daemon's
# plugin and AuthZ code, which the panel does not run; the SDK only imports
# the packages. Remove when a fixed release is published and adopted.
GO-2026-4887
GO-2026-4883

# gorilla/websocket v1.5.3, the newest tag: a client's frame mask key comes
# from math/rand (conn.go, newMaskKey). v1.5.1 and v1.5.2 read crypto/rand
# and v1.5.3 went back; after it the fix is on an untagged commit only
# (v1.5.4-0.20240701034025-d67f41855da4). Accepted: math/rand's top-level
# functions are randomly seeded since Go 1.20 (Toft builds with 1.26, where
# they read the runtime's generator), and the only client is the agent's
# dial to its panel (cmd/toft-agent/run.go; ws:// when the panel's address
# is http), where the mask key isn't a protection: it keeps a browser's page
# from choosing the bytes a caching proxy sees, and the agent's frames
# carry SSH (pkg/wsconn). Check for a release after v1.5.3 on 2026-12-18;
# remove the line when one is adopted.
GO-2026-6278

# Not listed, and not to be: GO-2026-5617, GO-2026-5668 and GO-2026-5746
# (docker cp and the archive endpoint; no fixed release either). They name
# functions of the daemon package, which the backend doesn't import, so
# govulncheck doesn't report them as reached and a line here would be
# called stale. The engine on a server is internal/advisory/known.go's.
